    "findings": [
      "Pure report model/validation/serialization layer; no file writing, network I/O, scheduling, cache execution or authority path is present in the package.",
      "createReportMetadata defaults generatedAt from host Date and preserves optional-field omission; generator and metadata objects are caller-provided and reference/alias behavior is observable.",
      "Constructors default arrays/counts with nullish semantics, normalize the metadata kind and preserve report-specific literals such as correctnessRequiredCache:false; mutable input arrays and nested reports are retained.",
      "summarizeDiagnostics counts exact severity strings and derives critical/error/warning/ok priority; status formatting and diagnostic order are part of the contract.",
      "validateLoReport traverses discriminated report kinds and checks names, metadata, diagnostics, counts and redaction fields; malformed unions, missing fields, sparse arrays and proxies require differential treatment.",
      "createProcessingReport and cache/storage reports describe recovery, quarantine and conservative fallbacks but do not perform retries, quarantine, eviction or cache correctness enforcement.",
      "serializeReportJson relies on JSON.stringify and can expose or transform caller data according to normal JSON semantics; it is not a redaction or signing boundary.",
      "The existing report-status Fungi asset proves only the bounded selectReportStatus priority cube and does not replace the complete TypeScript module or grant consumer authority.",
      "No new Fungi twin or queue admission is authorized; TypeScript remains the consumer shadow."
    ]
  },
